# File Feedback

I've reviewed this file and have 14 pieces of feedback:

## 1. (line 75) Feedback on: "obsolete optional names are rejected"
> What do you mean by this? If you're hinting that some backwards compatibility was preserved in the code, then know i do not want back compat anywhere

## 2. (lines 87–104) Feedback on: "prompts once everyone is ready."
> "...once everyone is ready. Pass `true` if most of the team should stay put in the beginning besides a minority with a head start."

( if you can simplify this sentence I added for more streamlined English that would be great)

## 3. (line 106) [👍 Looks good] Feedback on: "description

You are automatically part of the team as main. Do not include yourself in teammates. Use team_resume to continue an existing team, or team_add_teammates to grow one.
promptSnippet

Spawn a versatile team of agents"

## 4. (line 118) Feedback on: "JSON text with StartResult. The teammate array contains the newly created members. No initial status map or separate sessions map. started is false for an idle or empty team."
> I want the data about teammates to be Same pattern: `Required<Teammate> & { teammateId, sessionFile, live }`.
does This make the `TeammateIdentity` type obsolete? (because `Teammate` already includes the name). if so, let's remove `TeammateIdentity`.

## 5. (lines 176–193) Feedback on: "team_resume({
  // Team name or persistent ID
  team: string;
  // Optionally pick which teammates to resume, by name. Omit to resume all stopped teammates.
  // Schema: minimum items: 1.
  teammates?: string[];"
> Add a todo comment: "Should allow defining new teammates or even existing teammates (any Pi session ID belonging to this project) from other teams and sessions for maximum flexibility." and a second TODO: "Should support specifying teammate names or teammate ID’s all the same"

## 6. (lines 176–193) Feedback on: "startIdle?: boolean;"
> if startIdle is specified true, and for any reason, any teammate is active upon resumption (for example, the teammate had already existed and has been doing things at the time of resumption), the called of `team_resume` should know about this. it's still a success result, but the success object should let it know which "teammates { name, id } are active at the time of resumption because they had existed before and have been active at time of resumption"

## 7. (line 209) Feedback on: "Each returned teammate also has contextRestored: boolean"
> When is contextRestored: false?

## 8. (line 209) Feedback on: "Only members actually resumed appear in teammates"
> So idle teammates are transparent to consumers of this StartResult? 
What about already-live teammates?
`teammates` should return all of the team‘s teammates, just like `team_list` returns exhaustive information about the entire team. Same pattern: `Required<Teammate> & {teammateId, sessionFile live}`. Here, i am *assuming* `live` means `idle` or `active`, right?
also, i've we're doing `Required<Teammate> & {teammateId, sessionFile live}`, does this strengthen the claim that StartResult is obsolete?

## 9. (line 209) Feedback on: "started is false for idle or no-op resume."
> `started` should be false only for all teammates idle. anything else, even if one teammate is resumed because it has been active all along (what you call a "no-op" resume), should qualify as `started: true`. 

## 10. (lines 219–230) Feedback on: "// New teammates to add"
> Tell me, if an existing Pi session ID is specified here (given it belongs to the current project), does the current implementation handle it all the same now? Assigning that teammate to the team. If so, then change the parameter description to:
`// Teammates to add. Can be new you define, and any existing Pi session belonging to the current project. `

## 11. (line 244) Feedback on: "Only newly added members appear in teammates"
> should be all teammates. Here, I'm ok with returning `teammates` as an array of objects as defined in `StartResult`, because there's no need to be so comprehensive with full load for each teammate. Lightweight is good here.

## 12. (lines 256–268) Feedback on: "team_send_message({
  // Team name; optional only when exactly one team exists
  team?: string;
  // Recipient teammate names
  to: string[];
  // Message to send
  message: string;
  // True interrupts every recipient. A list interrupts only those names, which must also appear in
  // to. False or omitted interrupts none.
  interrupt?: boolean | string[];
});"
> same issue as the other place: The relationship between the team param and the individual teammates list `to` is confusing. Is it mutually exclusive? Specifying a team and no teammates is equivalent to specifying all this team's teammates? this structure is to prevent ambiguity when teammates from different teams have the same name? i can smell a simplification win here to

## 13. (lines 430–435) Feedback on: "get_context_window_usage({
  // Teammate names. Use an empty list to get only your own usage.
  targets: string[];
});"
> what happens in case teammaets from different teams have the same name? 

## 14. (lines 483–502) Feedback on: "team_log({
  // Team name; optional only when exactly one team exists
  team?: string;
  // Filter to one teammate name
  teammate?: string;"
> The relationship between the team param and the individual teammates list params is confusing. Is it mutually exclusive? Additive? Specifying a team and no teammates is equivalent to specifying all this team's teammates? What if i want to check the context of two teammates with the same name from different teams? i think a minimal API change is justified, not just docs. feels like there's a simplification win that fixes it

---

